{
  "abstract": "We exclude six infinite sequences of bisections of the exotic-quintuple surface of Dujella, Kazalicki and Petričević. Let $Q$ be the known rational section of its elliptic quotient. For every positive odd integer $s$ and every $\\ell\\in\\{3,5,7\\}$, no translate of $nQ$ by rational two-torsion gives a nondegenerate rational lift when $2n-1=\\ell s^2$ or $\\ell^2s^2$. This follows from three seed obstructions and a uniform division-polynomial argument. The seed square conditions at $2Q$, $3Q$ and $4Q$ have hyperelliptic models of genera five, seventeen and thirty-five; we prove that each has exactly eight rational points, all above $r=0,\\pm1,\\infty$. The first maps to a rank-zero elliptic curve. The second maps to a genus-four curve whose five rational points we classify using certified descent and three-adic Chabauty at Jacobian rank two. The third maps to a genus-eight curve of rank seven; one annihilating differential excludes precisely the disks reachable through $u=r^2+r^{-2}$. A generic identity then expresses the remaining square condition through an odd division polynomial. Nonsingular-reduction valuation propagation forces any lift in the stated sequences to satisfy one of the impossible seed square conditions, including at the relevant multiplicative primes. Independent divisor arithmetic, explicit local witnesses, anchor checks and analytic error bounds support the calculations. A source-only supplement regenerates the finite certificates and the hypotheses of the uniform argument. We do not exclude all multiples, arbitrary multisections, or rational Diophantine septuples.",
